  "id": "COMPOUND:7223 - PROTEIN:4145",
  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (1S,7S,8S,8AR)-1,2,3,7,8,8A-HEXAHYDRO-7-METHYL-8-[2-[(2R,4R)-TETRAHYDRO-4-HYDROXY-6-OXO-2H-PYRAN-2-YL]ETHYL]-1-NAPHTHALENOL, is strongly associated with Protein Nef through multiple pathways. It is a known target of Myxopyronin B, which itself is a compound that interacts with the protein Nef. This relationship is supported by multiple evidence chains, each linking the compound to Myxopyronin B and then to Nef. The compound is also shown to target other proteins, such as Alpha-pyrone synthesis polyketide synthase-like Pks18 and Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2B catalytic subunit alpha isoform, all of which are targets of Myxopyronin B. These findings suggest that the compound may exert its biological effects through interactions with Myxopyronin B, which in turn modulates Protein Nef. The evidence is consistent and strong, indicating a potential mechanism by which the compound influences Protein Nef, likely through the action of Myxopyronin B.",
